  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "body": "Apply when replacing immediate document writes with a reusable trailing task. TASK: \"Coalesce edits using the existing trailing-task utility: after a 120 ms quiet\\ninterval, write only the latest text in that editing burst. Subsequent bursts\\nmust continue to save.\" Check that edits replace pending text and restart the document's 120 ms interval.",
      "category": "applicability"
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "body": "Bind pending work to the document selected when the edit occurs, and retain that document's buffer in the coordinator dictionary. docs/host-api.md: \"Document buffers are owned by the coordinator dictionary, while Badge owns only a live subscription.\" src/workflow.go binds save identity with \"NewTrailing(w.env,120,func(text string){w.env.Write(id,text)})\". A deferred save must not select its destination from whatever badge happens to be current when the timer fires.",
      "category": "event_relation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "body": "Consume pending task state before invoking callback-capable work. src/workflow.go: \"if t.handle!=nil { t.env.Cancel(t.handle) };text:=t.pending;t.handle=nil;t.pending=nil\" followed by \"if text!=nil { t.work(*text) }\". Preserve this ordering so a completed flush cannot retain consumed text or erase work queued synchronously by its callback.",
      "category": "event_relation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R04",
      "body": "Preserve document persistence when navigation detaches a badge. TASK: \"Preserve the editor's other behavior and public interfaces.\" README.md: \"A workspace document buffer persists independently of the current view badge.\" The original edit writes synchronously in src/workflow.go: \"func(w *Workspace)Edit(text string){view:=w.current;if view!=nil{w.env.Write(view.id,text)}}\". When introducing delay, check that pending departing-document text is persisted before departure returns rather than discarded with the subscription.",
      "category": "preservation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R05",
      "body": "Treat saving as a synchronous reentry boundary. docs/host-api.md: \"A store listener may call navigation synchronously.\" src/workflow.go records \"request:=w.generation\" before retirement and checks \"if true&&request!=w.generation{return}\" afterward. Keep the supersession check after callback-capable departure work and before installing the requested badge or publishing its document, so an older navigation cannot overwrite a newer nested request.",
      "category": "event_relation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R06",
      "body": "Keep subscription cleanup separate from document-buffer ownership. src/workflow.go: \"func(b *Badge)detach(){b.env.Store().Stop(b.token)}\". Detaching a badge should release its live subscription while coordinator-owned pending persistence remains accounted for. Preserve source payload semantics: docs/host-api.md states \"All source identities/text and status payloads retain original semantics.\"",
      "category": "preservation"
    },
    {
      "id": "R07",
      "body": "Exclude transient discard-on-hide workflows from the document departure rule. TASK: \"The adjacent search preview is outside this maintenance change.\" src/workflow.go gives preview its own delay with \"NewTrailing(env,40,func(query string){env.Output(\\\"preview\\\",Value{\\\"query\\\":query})})\" and cancellation with \"func(p *Preview)Hide(){p.task.Cancel()}\". Preserve its 40 ms timing, discard behavior, and later reuse.",
      "category": "exclusion"
    },
    {
      "id": "R08",
      "body": "Verify distinct behaviors with controlled timers and synchronous listeners: no burst write before 120 ms of quiet; one latest-text write afterward; a subsequent burst saves; pending departure text persists through Open, Close, and Dispose; navigation invoked during saving remains authoritative; preview cancellation and reuse remain unchanged. TASK supports repeated saves with \"Subsequent bursts\\nmust continue to save.\" src/workflow.go connects disposal to closing with \"func(w *Workspace)Dispose(){w.Close()}\". These checks exercise source-supported obligations without making observed outputs new requirements.",
      "category": "verification"
    }
  ],
